#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device.rst:7
msgid "Xe Device Wedging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:9: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c:1387
msgid ""
"Xe driver uses drm device wedged uevent as documented in Documentation/gpu/"
"drm-uapi.rst. When device is in wedged state, every IOCTL will be blocked "
"and GT cannot be used. The conditions under which the driver declares the "
"device wedged depend on the wedged mode configuration (see :c:type:`enum "
"xe_wedged_mode <xe_wedged_mode>`). The default recovery method for a wedged "
"state is rebind/bus-reset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:9: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c:1393
msgid ""
"Another recovery method is vendor-specific. Below are the cases that send "
"``WEDGED=vendor-specific`` recovery method in drm device wedged uevent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:9: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c:1402
msgid ""
"``WEDGED=vendor-specific`` drm device wedged uevent with :ref:`Runtime "
"Survivability mode <xe-survivability-mode>` is used to notify admin/"
"userspace consumer about the need for a firmware flash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:9: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c:1409
msgid ""
"Once ``WEDGED=vendor-specific`` drm device wedged uevent is received, follow "
"the below steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:9: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c:1412
msgid ""
"Check Runtime Survivability mode sysfs. If enabled, firmware flash is "
"required to recover the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:9: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c:1415
msgid "/sys/bus/pci/devices/<device>/survivability_mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:9: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_device.c:1417
msgid ""
"Admin/userspace consumer can use firmware flashing tools like fwupd to flash "
"firmware and restore device to normal operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device.rst:14
msgid "GPU Health Indicator"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:638
msgid ""
"On Intel Xe platforms that support the gpu health indicator interface, the "
"driver exposes this sysfs attribute for in-band access to the gpu health "
"state::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:644
msgid ""
"Reading the attribute is available to all users and returns a single line "
"containing the current gpu health state, whereas writing is restricted to "
"administrative users and updates the state to one of the valid values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:649
msgid ""
"Management tools and administrators use this interface to query the current "
"gpu health state (e.g. for telemetry/monitoring) and to update it - for "
"example, to mark the gpu as ``warning`` or ``critical`` after diagnostics, "
"or reset it back to ``ok`` once remediated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:654
msgid "The valid values for the gpu health state are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:656
msgid "``ok``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:657
msgid "The gpu is healthy and operating within normal parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:659
msgid "``warning``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:660
msgid "The gpu is experiencing minor issues but remains operational."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:662
msgid "``critical``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:663
msgid "The gpu is in a critical state and may not be operational."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_device:16: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_ras.c:665
msgid ""
"See Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-intel-xe-ras for the ABI "
"specification."
msgstr ""
